// Adversarial: Haste hazard active at 4 stacks in a Corridor layout, driving the bolt
// speed reconciliation loop under high wall-bounce frequency.
//
// haste_apply_speed runs every FixedUpdate tick and reconciles each Bolt's
// EffectStack<SpeedBoostConfig> by retaining the hazard:haste source entry and pushing
// the current multiplier. At 4 stacks the multiplier is 1 + (0.20 + 3*0.10) = 1.50,
// adding 50% speed on top of whatever chip/protocol boosts exist. The Corridor layout
// forces hundreds of wall bounces per run — each bounce re-enters the speed clamp
// path. This stresses:
//   - BoltSpeedAccurate: if haste_apply_speed double-applies or forgets to retain_by_source
//     before pushing, speed accumulates multiplicatively and escapes BoltMaxSpeed.
//   - NoNaN: multiplier arithmetic on large stack counts could produce inf or NaN if
//     the formula is mis-scaled.
//   - BoltInBounds: extreme speed without clamping pushes the bolt outside bounds.
//
// Adversarial conditions:
//   - 4 stacks: exercises per_level_percent scaling beyond stack 1
//   - Corridor layout: maximises wall bounces and speed-clamp re-entries per run
//   - Chaos input (0.7): breaker movement variability forces the speed system to
//     reconcile under all bump-quality distributions
//   - BoltSpeedAccurate: primary detector for multiplier double-application
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Corridor",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 8000,
    disallowed_failures: [BoltInBounds, BoltSpeedAccurate, BreakerCountReasonable, BreakerInBounds, BreakerPositionClamped, NoNaN],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    seed: 7722,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 30, mutation: InjectHazardStack(kind_name: "Haste", stacks: 4)),
    ],
)
